@startuml uc001-analysis-sequence
!include ../../../diagrams/style.iuml
title UC-001 Configure model connections: analysis sequence (main success scenario)

boundary "Configuration Interface" as CI
control "Configure Connection" as Conf
entity "Connection Profile" as CP
boundary "Environment Interface" as EI
control "Call Model" as Call
boundary "Provider Interface" as PI
entity "Model Response" as MR

CI -> Conf : settings for "target" (then "judge")
Conf -> CP : create(name, provider, model, key variable,\nbase URL, timeout, retries, options)
CP -> CP : validate every setting,\ncollect every problem
Conf -> Conf : choose the connector for the profile's provider
Conf -> EI : read variable(key variable name)
EI --> Conf : key, trimmed
Conf -> Call : configure(model, key, base URL,\ntimeout, retries, options)

[-> Call : call(prompt, instructions)
Call -> PI : one request, instructions\nin the provider's own way
PI --> Call : answer or refusal, served model,\nfinish reason, usage, request id
Call -> MR : create(text or refusal, requested and served model,\nfinish reason, truncated, token counts, request id)
[<-- Call : model response

note right of PI
  5a, 6b: a failure or an untrustworthy
  reply becomes a Connector Error
  of a known kind. 6a: a refusal is
  a Model Response, not an error.
end note
@enduml
